# Portal Kit

Portal Kit renders navigation state for a small documentation site.

The default visual theme is light for visitors without a saved preference.
Breadcrumbs appear above the page title on every documentation page.
The skip link targets the `main-content` landmark.
from .config import DEFAULT_THEME
from .navigation import breadcrumb, skip_link


def render_page(title, sections, theme=None):
    trail = breadcrumb(["docs", title])
    links = "".join(f"<li>{section}</li>" for section in sections)
    return (
        skip_link()
        + f'<main id="main-content" data-theme="{theme or DEFAULT_THEME}">'
        + f"<nav>{trail}</nav><h1>{title}</h1><ul>{links}</ul></main>"
    )
def breadcrumb(parts):
    return " / ".join(part.strip().title() for part in parts)


def skip_link(target="main-content"):
    return f'<a class="skip" href="#{target}">Skip to content</a>'
# Accessibility

Keyboard focus uses a three-pixel blue outline with a two-pixel offset.
Navigation labels must remain visible at widths below 640 pixels.
Every rendered page exposes exactly one main landmark.
.skip:focus {
  outline: 3px solid blue;
  outline-offset: 2px;
}

@media (max-width: 639px) {
  nav { display: block; }
}

